74,1278,1279],{"class":1144}," app",[774,1281,987],{"class":1103},[774,1283,1141],{"class":1103},[774,1285,1286],{"class":1144}," baseURL",[774,1288,987],{"class":1103},[774,1290,1132],{"class":1103},[774,1292,1293],{"class":783},"\u002Fexamples",[774,1295,1104],{"class":1103},[774,1297,1171],{"class":1103},[774,1299,1171],{"class":1103},[774,1301,1174],{"class":1112},[774,1303,1177],{"class":1103},[1305,1306,1307,1328,1339],"ul",{},[1308,1309,1310,1311,1314,1315,1318,1319,1318,1322,1318,1325,1081],"li",{},"The third argument is env, read by the fixture's ",[771,1312,1313],{},"nuxt.config.ts"," (",[771,1316,1317],{},"BASIC_VARIANT",", ",[771,1320,1321],{},"SEO_VARIANT",[771,1323,1324],{},"STRATEGY",[771,1326,1327],{},"TRANSLATION_PAYLOADS",[1308,1329,1330,1331,1334,1335,1338],{},"The fourth is a ",[771,1332,1333],{},"nuxtConfig"," override, for a global URL shape. It is a defu merge, so arrays concatenate: never pass ",[771,1336,1337],{},"locales"," that way, switch them by env.",[1308,1340,1341,1342,1318,1344,915,1346,1348],{},"A suite that builds a fixture itself (",[771,1343,926],{},[771,1345,914],{},[771,1347,918],{},") sets the same env as the recipe.",[748,1350,1351,1352,1355,1356,1359],{},"Builds are hashed by fixture directory and ",[771,1353,1354],{},"src\u002F",", cached in ",[771,1357,1358],{},"test\u002F.untestutils\u002Fbuilds"," (CI caches that directory) and started once per run.",[759,1361,1363],{"id":1362},"parallel-builds","Parallel builds",[1305,1365,1366,1384,1404],{},[1308,1367,1368,923,1372,1375,1376,1379,1380,1383],{},[1369,1370,1371],"strong",{},"Own build dir per suite.",[771,1373,1374],{},"isolatedBuild(fixture, name)"," points ",[771,1377,1378],{},"NUXT_TEST_BUILD_DIR"," at ",[771,1381,1382],{},"test\u002F.fixture-builds\u002F\u003Cfixture>\u002F\u003Cname>\u002F",", outside the fixture: a build written into it would change the recipe hash mid-run.",[1308,1385,1386,1389,1390,1314,1393,1396,1397,1314,1400,1403],{},[1369,1387,1388],{},"OS-assigned ports."," Take ports from ",[771,1391,1392],{},"getFreePort()",[771,1394,1395],{},"test\u002Fhelpers\u002Fport.ts",") and stop servers with ",[771,1398,1399],{},"stopChild()",[771,1401,1402],{},"test\u002Fhelpers\u002Fsubprocess.ts","), which kills the whole process group. Never free a port by killing whatever owns it: with parallel workers that can kill a sibling suite's server.",[1308,1405,1406,1409,1410,972,1413,757],{},[1369,1407,1408],{},"No writes inside the repo tree."," Specs that edit locale files or start a server from the build output run on a temp copy from ",[771,1411,1412],{},"tmpFixture()",[771,1414,1415],{},"test\u002Fhelpers\u002Ftmp-fixture.ts",[748,1417,1418,1419,1422,1423,1113,1426,1429,1430,1433,1434,1437],{},"Each strategy has one file, ",[771,1420,1421],{},"test\u002Fstrategies-\u003Cstrategy>.test.ts",", so Vitest runs all four at once. They share ",[771,1424,1425],{},"test\u002Fhelpers\u002Fstrategy-suite.ts",[771,1427,1428],{},"nuxi generate"," into an isolated build, then the output is read from disk. It is one chain (a single ",[771,1431,1432],{},"test","), so a strategy costs one build. The server side of the same routes is checked by ",[771,1435,1436],{},"test\u002Fjourneys\u002Fstrategies-*.spec.ts"," on the recipe's server build.",[759,1439,1441],{"id":1440},"journeys","Journeys",[748,1443,1444,1445,1451],{},"Browser e2e runs through ",[755,1446,1450],{"href":1447,"rel":1448},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fs00d\u002Funtestutils",[1449],"nofollow","untestutils"," and a real Playwright browser.",[1305,1453,1454,1461,1472,1498,1518],{},[1308,1455,1456,1457,1460],{},"One spec walks one real flow on one recipe: visit, browse, switch locale, reload, detection, head. Each step has a ",[771,1458,1459],{},"\u002F\u002F step n: action → assert"," comment.",[1308,1462,1463,1464,1467,1468,1471],{},"One harness per file: ",[771,1465,1466],{},"test.override({ harness: '\u003Crecipe>' })"," at the top of the ",[771,1469,1470],{},"describe",". A second harness in the same file would reach the first one's server, so split it into its own file.",[1308,1473,1474,1475,1478,1479,1482,1483,1486,1487,1490,1491,1494,1495,757],{},"No ",[771,1476,1477],{},"waitForTimeout",", no ",[771,1480,1481],{},"networkidle",", no optional ",[771,1484,1485],{},"if"," assertions. Statuses come from ",[771,1488,1489],{},"request.get(path)",", with ",[771,1492,1493],{},"{ maxRedirects: 0 }"," where the redirect itself is checked. Arm console collectors before the first ",[771,1496,1497],{},"goto",[1308,1499,1500,1501,1503,1504,1507,1508,1511,1512,1515,1516,757],{},"Specs import ",[771,1502,1432],{}," from ",[771,1505,1506],{},"test\u002Fhelpers\u002Fguarded-test.ts",". It fails a test on any document response >= 500, uncaught page error, console error or hydration warning, even when the assertions pass. A test that expects one calls ",[771,1509,1510],{},"guard.allow(\u002Fpattern\u002F)","; ",[771,1513,1514],{},"test.override({ guardAllow: [\u002Fpattern\u002F] })"," allows a pattern for a whole ",[771,1517,1470],{},[1308,1519,1520,1521,1524],{},"Retries cover infrastructure only (",[771,1522,1523],{},"retryInfra",", CI): a failing assertion fails.",[759,1526,1528],{"id":1527},"routing-goldens","Routing goldens",[748,1530,1531,1534,1535,1538,1539,1318,1542,1318,1545,1548],{},[771,1532,1533],{},"test\u002Frouting-characterization"," runs every app in ",[771,1536,1537],{},"scenarios.ts"," under every strategy and records what each URL reads as and where each navigation lands. The harness calls the code the module calls (",[771,1540,1541],{},"mergeDefineI18nRouteMeta",[771,1543,1544],{},"extractDefineI18nRouteData",[771,1546,1547],{},"RouteGenerator","), so do not copy module logic into it: a copy cannot fail.",[1305,1550,1551,1569,1576],{},[1308,1552,1553,1554,1557,1558,1561,1562,1565,1566,1081],{},"Pages are not only what the file scanner makes: ",[771,1555,1556],{},"modulePages"," are pushed as in ",[771,1559,1560],{},"pages:extend",", with or without a name, and ",[771,1563,1564],{},"noPages"," runs Nuxt's stub router with no records (",[771,1567,1568],{},"pages: false",[1308,1570,1571,1572,1575],{},"Input is frozen, so a package that writes to pages or routes throws in the golden. Every page is tagged with its file, and a record that loses ",[771,1573,1574],{},"meta"," is listed under the invariant breaks.",[1308,1577,1578],{},"A golden diff is either an intended fix or a bug. Read all of it before you regenerate.",[759,1580,1582],{"id":1581},"mutation-testing","Mutation testing",[748,1584,1585,1588,1589,1594,1595,1598,1599,1602],{},[771,1586,1587],{},"pnpm run test:mutation"," runs ",[755,1590,1593],{"href":1591,"rel":1592},"https:\u002F\u002Fstryker-mutator.io\u002F",[1449],"Stryker"," on one package. It changes the source (",[771,1596,1597],{},"\u003C"," to ",[771,1600,1601],{},"\u003C=",", a branch removed, a string emptied) and reruns the tests that cover the change; a surviving mutant is a behaviour no test pins.",[764,1604,1606],{"className":766,"code":1605,"language":768,"meta":769,"style":769},"MUTATE_PACKAGE=core pnpm run test:mutation                      # score; JSON report in test-results\u002Fmutation\u002F\nMUTATE_PACKAGE=core MUTATE_ALL_KILLERS=1 pnpm run test:mutation # record every test that kills each mutant\n",[771,1607,1608,1629],{"__ignoreMap":769},[774,1609,1610,1613,1616,1618,1621,1623,1626],{"class":776,"line":353},[774,1611,1612],{"class":1112},"MUTATE_PACKAGE",[774,1614,1615],{"class":1103},"=",[774,1617,218],{"class":783},[774,1619,1620],{"class":779}," pnpm",[774,1622,784],{"class":783},[774,1624,1625],{"class":783}," test:mutation",[774,1627,1628],{"class":790},"                      # score; JSON report in test-results\u002Fmutation\u002F\n",[774,1630,1631,1633,1635,1637,1640,1642,1645,1647,1649,1651],{"class":776,"line":794},[774,1632,1612],{"class":1112},[774,1634,1615],{"class":1103},[774,1636,218],{"class":783},[774,1638,1639],{"class":1112}," MUTATE_ALL_KILLERS",[774,1641,1615],{"class":1103},[774,1643,1644],{"class":783},"1",[774,1646,1620],{"class":779},[774,1648,784],{"class":783},[774,1650,1625],{"class":783},[774,1652,1653],{"class":790}," # record every test that kills each mutant\n",[748,1655,1656,1657,1660],{},"With ",[771,1658,1659],{},"MUTATE_ALL_KILLERS=1"," the report lists every killing test per mutant, so a test whose mutants are all killed by others can be deleted. Package tests are kept to a small set that still kills every mutant any test kills. New tests are scenarios (set up like a real app, act, assert, act again), not one-line checks.",[759,1662,1664],{"id":1663},"related","Related",[1666,1667,1668,1673,1675],"card-group",{},[1669,1670],"card",{"icon":1671,"title":320,"to":1672},"i-lucide-git-pull-request","\u002Fcontributing\u002F",[1669,1674],{"icon":1671,"title":335,"to":336},[1669,1676],{"icon":1677,"title":115,"to":116},"i-lucide-book-open",[1679,1680,1681],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;--shiki-dark:#FFCB6B}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html pre.shiki code .sHwdD, html code.shiki .sHwdD{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-default:#546E7A;--shiki-default-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#676E95;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);f